Description: Disable the in-app update checker
 snapd owns updates for this snap through the Snap Store, and this
 build must never contact an outside host on its own. UpdateManager::
 startCheck() is the single chokepoint every check and download leads back
 to: checkForUpdates() (the manual action), maybeCheckAutomatically() (the
 startup timer) and downloadUpdate() (gated on reaching the UpdateAvailable
 state, itself only reachable from a successful check) all go through it.
 Refusing there unconditionally, ahead of its own development-build and
 trust-key gates, disables every path at once, including the
 LIGHTNING_ALLOW_DEV_UPDATE_CHECK diagnostic override.
 .
 Also adds UpdateManager::checksDisabledByPolicy (reading the same
 kChecksDisabledByPolicy flag startCheck() refuses from) and uses it in
 qml/UpdatesSettingsSection.qml to replace the "Automatic checks" toggle
 and the "Check for updates" button with a fixed notice, and to hide every
 check-result state in the "Status" card (Idle/Checking/UpToDate/
 UpdateAvailable/Downloading/Verifying/ReadyToInstall/Installing/
 RestartRequired/Failed). Without this, the automatic startup timer still
 flips the backend to Failed every launch (harmlessly, with no network
 involved) and the pane would show that as an alarming, misleading error
 banner. updateLastResultBlock (the previous install's outcome, from the
 helper's status file) is unrelated to checking and is left alone.
Author: Erich Eickmeyer <eeickmeyer@ubuntu.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-23

